    {
      "id": "8c288a76-33c8-4e01-b67a-10e2f20ed3b3",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -304,
        -48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 528,
        "height": 944,
        "content": "## Linkedin Poster from Knowledge Base\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow keeps a Supabase-backed knowledge base in sync with files from Google Drive, then periodically uses that knowledge base to create LinkedIn content. New files are downloaded, extracted, chunked, embedded with Google Gemini, and stored in Supabase; updated files first have their old rows deleted before being re-indexed. On a schedule, an AI agent combines company knowledge with Tavily web search, generates structured post content, creates an image with Gemini, and publishes the final result to LinkedIn.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect Google Drive credentials and configure the new-file and updated-file triggers to watch the correct folder or files.\n- Configure Supabase credentials, the vector table, matching metadata fields such as file_id, and the delete-row logic used when files are updated.\n- Add Google Gemini credentials for chat, embeddings, and image generation nodes.\n- Add Tavily credentials for the web search tool used by the AI agent.\n- Connect LinkedIn credentials and choose the target personal profile or organization page for publishing.\n- Review the AI agent prompt, structured output schema, schedule frequency, and Google Drive file ID mappings before activating the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the schedule, LinkedIn post prompt, image style prompt, Tavily search behavior, text splitter chunk settings, and Supabase vector table or metadata schema to match the brand voice and knowledge base structure."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
